WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.959 --> 00:00:04.590
We have a great phrase
today on the Bloomberg

00:00:04.590 --> 00:00:06.460
talking about a year of fire and ice.

00:00:06.460 --> 00:00:08.870
The decade began really
with everything crumbling

00:00:08.870 --> 00:00:10.320
and a lot of panic.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:14.300
And now we're sort of
heading into a new year

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:16.370
when apparently nothing can go wrong.

00:00:17.828 --> 00:00:20.420
There was some feeling in The White House

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:23.960
that this virus was so
contagious that it was almost

00:00:23.960 --> 00:00:27.390
inevitable that people
were going to get it.

00:00:27.390 --> 00:00:32.390
For weeks and weeks, China
and the WHO was downplaying

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:33.460
what was happening.

00:00:34.880 --> 00:00:38.520
There was resistance To
impose a strict lockdown

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:41.733
because it's one of the
industrial hubs of Italy.

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:46.980
The outbreak itself is
unprecedented but divisiveness

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.913
in which it is evolving is unprecedented.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.870
The idea back then that a
vaccine would be the way out

00:00:53.870 --> 00:00:58.489
of this was quite crazy at the beginning.

00:00:58.489 --> 00:01:00.130
We have it totally under control,

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:02.563
it's one person coming in from China.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:06.543
We have to operate in a political context.

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.003
We were in uncharted territory.

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.463
Everything we did was right.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.770
2020 was a year like no other.

00:01:44.770 --> 00:01:48.450
It was a tale of government
missteps, missed opportunities

00:01:48.450 --> 00:01:51.950
to contain the virus and
mixed messaging that left many

00:01:51.950 --> 00:01:55.423
uncertain of the risks
and divided on the cures.

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.490
2021 begins with reasons for optimism

00:02:01.490 --> 00:02:04.680
but experts see more viral threats ahead.

00:02:04.680 --> 00:02:07.680
If we have any hope to bring
an end to this pandemic,

00:02:07.680 --> 00:02:10.410
in which at least 2
million are expected to die

00:02:10.410 --> 00:02:13.760
and protect against future
outbreaks, we need to understand

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:16.700
what went wrong with our global response.

00:02:16.700 --> 00:02:18.497
Starting at the beginning.

00:02:28.870 --> 00:02:32.580
I still remember the first
time we saw a report,

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:36.090
actually stock started tanking
because there was this rumor

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:39.930
circulating online that there
was a mysterious pneumonia

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:41.270
that was detected in Wuhan.

00:02:41.270 --> 00:02:44.170
There is growing concern across Asia,

00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:47.460
as the Wuhan pneumonia
outbreak continues to spread.

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.713
I'd actually just come back from Wuhan

00:02:49.713 --> 00:02:51.380
reporting on a separate story.

00:02:51.380 --> 00:02:53.670
And I still remember us joking about,

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:55.310
good thing you didn't
fall sick and you know,

00:02:55.310 --> 00:02:57.130
we hope you didn't catch anything.

00:02:57.130 --> 00:02:59.560
In early January, hospitals in Wuhan

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.540
faced an onslaught of
severely sick patients

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:05.290
and antibiotic treatments weren't working.

00:03:05.290 --> 00:03:08.500
The local healthcare system
started to break down.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:12.020
We sent a couple of headlines
and we were kind of like,

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.560
oh wouldn't it be crazy
if there was another SARS.

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:17.280
China has announced the
first death from an outbreak

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:20.770
of pneumonia caused by
an unidentified virus.

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.370
By January 10th, Chinese
scientists have mapped

00:03:23.370 --> 00:03:26.180
out the genetic makeup of
the virus that will be shared

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:29.060
with infectious disease experts worldwide.

00:03:29.060 --> 00:03:32.900
At that time, 41 people were
diagnosed with the virus.

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:37.650
It was a gradual evolution and awareness

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:39.930
of just how bad it could be.

00:03:39.930 --> 00:03:44.400
It went from a curiosity to
over a period of a few months,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:46.153
an impending disaster.

00:03:47.190 --> 00:03:49.490
Within weeks the pathogen is running riot

00:03:49.490 --> 00:03:52.053
throughout Wuhan's
population of 11 million.

00:03:52.053 --> 00:03:55.343
As well as the broader central
Chinese province of Hubei.

00:03:56.220 --> 00:04:01.010
And then on January 23rd,
they shut down Wuhan.

00:04:01.010 --> 00:04:04.423
And that was the moment we
knew that it was serious.

00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:14.100
A city of 11 million
people with almost no one

00:04:14.100 --> 00:04:15.040
on the streets.

00:04:15.040 --> 00:04:17.060
People in Wuhan have
been asked not to leave

00:04:17.060 --> 00:04:20.563
the city and outsiders have
been told to stay away.

00:04:22.160 --> 00:04:25.430
It took effect at 10:00 a.m. the next day.

00:04:25.430 --> 00:04:29.510
Even people in Wuhan didn't
know what it really meant.

00:04:29.510 --> 00:04:33.183
It's kind of difficult to
get the perspective of how

00:04:33.183 --> 00:04:36.243
drastic a move that was back then.

00:04:37.090 --> 00:04:38.740
When that happened and they announced that

00:04:38.740 --> 00:04:41.000
they were quarantining
Wuhan, that was pretty much

00:04:41.000 --> 00:04:45.220
the biggest quarantine that
anybody had ever experienced

00:04:45.220 --> 00:04:46.313
in recent history.

00:04:47.380 --> 00:04:49.110
Groceries were flying off the shelves.

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:50.130
People were stocking up.

00:04:50.130 --> 00:04:51.560
People were trying to get out,

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:53.210
trying to get on the last train,

00:04:53.210 --> 00:04:55.240
trying to drive out of the city.

00:04:55.240 --> 00:04:57.910
There was a lot of confusing information.

00:04:57.910 --> 00:04:59.251
I wanted to get my medication

00:04:59.251 --> 00:05:01.550
but this pharmacy is closed.

00:05:01.550 --> 00:05:03.310
If the situation continues

00:05:03.310 --> 00:05:06.320
for one Or two more weeks,
it'll get more complicated.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.650
What took people by
surprise is that you know,

00:05:08.650 --> 00:05:10.810
the message on China for so long was that

00:05:10.810 --> 00:05:13.420
it was not a big deal and
suddenly they escalated it

00:05:13.420 --> 00:05:17.280
so abruptly with not laying
the groundwork with anybody.

00:05:17.280 --> 00:05:19.690
China's still uncontrolled viral outbreak

00:05:19.690 --> 00:05:23.500
comes just ahead of the week
long Lunar New Year holidays.

00:05:23.500 --> 00:05:26.850
It's the biggest annual
human migration in the world.

00:05:26.850 --> 00:05:30.860
When millions of tourists fan
out across Asia and Europe.

00:05:30.860 --> 00:05:33.380
Public health experts
feared a massive seeding

00:05:33.380 --> 00:05:35.800
of the virus across the globe.

00:05:35.800 --> 00:05:37.960
The government prevented a lot of people

00:05:37.960 --> 00:05:40.670
from returning to the cities
after Chinese New Year.

00:05:40.670 --> 00:05:42.750
And that really affected
a lot of people you know,

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:44.090
they weren't able to make money.

00:05:44.090 --> 00:05:47.050
They weren't able to
go back to their jobs.

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:48.940
And I think that that was
a really crucial moment

00:05:48.940 --> 00:05:52.010
in just establishing the fact
that we were in uncharted

00:05:52.010 --> 00:05:55.430
territory and that
everything going on was now

00:05:55.430 --> 00:05:59.373
on a level that had never
experienced for a long time.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.220
By the end of January,

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:04.683
the World Health Organization
declared the virus

00:06:04.683 --> 00:06:08.390
a public health emergency
of international concern.

00:06:08.390 --> 00:06:11.480
It wouldn't call it a
pandemic until March 11th.

00:06:11.480 --> 00:06:14.670
Some critics fault it for being too slow.

00:06:14.670 --> 00:06:18.240
A WHO official said the
organization had been sounding

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:21.003
the alarm well before
making its official call.

00:06:21.003 --> 00:06:23.550
Once you label something as a pandemic,

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:27.710
there is a tendency on the part
of certain groups of people

00:06:27.710 --> 00:06:31.860
to shrug their shoulders and
say, oh no, pandemic is here,

00:06:31.860 --> 00:06:34.850
we just might as well get
on and limit the damage

00:06:34.850 --> 00:06:36.450
as much as possible.

00:06:36.450 --> 00:06:39.720
Whereas the message that
we all wanted to convey

00:06:39.720 --> 00:06:44.420
from the end of January was,
this is a really nasty virus,

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.083
don't underestimate it.

00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.020
The most challenging part
of that initial phase

00:06:50.020 --> 00:06:53.670
of the crisis is that,
for weeks and weeks,

00:06:53.670 --> 00:06:58.220
China and the WHO who was
downplaying what was happening.

00:06:58.220 --> 00:07:00.990
Wuhan finally admitted those
human to human transmission

00:07:00.990 --> 00:07:02.718
but they were saying
there was not that much.

00:07:02.718 --> 00:07:04.423
WHO repeated that.

00:07:06.004 --> 00:07:07.780
At this point, the Chinese government

00:07:07.780 --> 00:07:11.070
was under heavy criticism for
not communicating effectively

00:07:11.070 --> 00:07:12.190
with the public.

00:07:12.190 --> 00:07:14.270
Releasing little information on the size

00:07:14.270 --> 00:07:16.200
and scope of the crisis.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:20.710
China wanted to keep people
from coming in to investigate

00:07:20.710 --> 00:07:23.280
the origin of the virus,
which is still an extremely

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:25.880
sensitive topic in China right now.

00:07:25.880 --> 00:07:28.200
The WHO was widely criticized

00:07:28.200 --> 00:07:30.920
by the international
community for praising China

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:33.250
in the early stages of the pandemic.

00:07:33.250 --> 00:07:36.990
But according to the
WHO, they had no choice.

00:07:36.990 --> 00:07:41.040
People who are given
responsibility in public health,

00:07:41.040 --> 00:07:44.970
we are not able just to
call the shots all the time.

00:07:44.970 --> 00:07:49.100
We have to operate in a political context.

00:07:49.100 --> 00:07:53.340
Our colleagues in China were
dealing with an acute problem.

00:07:53.340 --> 00:07:57.320
Were trying to collect data
about that acute problem.

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.630
Were trying also to
work inside the country

00:08:00.630 --> 00:08:02.690
on how severe it was.

00:08:02.690 --> 00:08:05.590
Were then deciding to close down a city

00:08:05.590 --> 00:08:09.083
of several million population
very, very quickly.

00:08:11.800 --> 00:08:14.060
A lot of China's missteps
came from the virus

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:16.720
being so new and no
country ever having dealt

00:08:16.720 --> 00:08:18.473
with such a situation before.

00:08:19.640 --> 00:08:23.570
China as a political system has a tendency

00:08:23.570 --> 00:08:25.700
towards nondisclosure.

00:08:25.700 --> 00:08:29.150
And when there is something
unknown they have a tendency

00:08:29.150 --> 00:08:31.800
to want things to be stable, to be quiet.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:34.510
They always err on the
side of not doing anything,

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:36.230
not saying anything.

00:08:36.230 --> 00:08:38.740
There was also a lot of
information leaking out

00:08:38.740 --> 00:08:41.630
on social media, some of
that would get censored.

00:08:41.630 --> 00:08:43.850
It's very difficult to tell what was real

00:08:43.850 --> 00:08:45.640
and what was not real.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:48.250
Public information about the novel virus,

00:08:48.250 --> 00:08:51.510
its symptoms and level of
contagiousness were limited.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:54.260
Some experts did try to raise the alarm.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:58.420
When Li Wenliang died, he
Was a doctor who had warned

00:08:58.420 --> 00:09:02.480
his former classmates and
his friends about a virus

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:06.110
that he had heard was spreading
and had made other doctors

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:08.660
sick and he was saying,
it could be another SARS

00:09:08.660 --> 00:09:10.780
and that everybody
should take precautions.

00:09:10.780 --> 00:09:12.800
And the government sanctioned him

00:09:12.800 --> 00:09:14.850
and other people in the WeChat group.

00:09:14.850 --> 00:09:18.640
That was really one of the
moments when it became clear

00:09:18.640 --> 00:09:21.500
to both the government and
the international community

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.440
just how much was at stake.

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:25.710
It wasn't just about containing the virus

00:09:25.710 --> 00:09:29.580
but it was what the virus stood
for which was whether or not

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:33.210
the Chinese system would
prevail and whether or not

00:09:33.210 --> 00:09:36.370
all of the things that people
give up would ultimately

00:09:36.370 --> 00:09:39.800
benefit them if it meant that
their government could contain

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:41.753
this deadly pandemic.

00:09:43.100 --> 00:09:44.930
China was also reluctant to let

00:09:44.930 --> 00:09:48.090
World Health Organization
infectious disease experts

00:09:48.090 --> 00:09:50.950
into the country until the
disease had already spread

00:09:50.950 --> 00:09:52.030
around the globe.

00:09:52.030 --> 00:09:55.590
The WHO ultimately did
send the team to China

00:09:55.590 --> 00:09:59.180
but the trip was extremely
tightly controlled

00:09:59.180 --> 00:10:00.250
by the government.

00:10:00.250 --> 00:10:04.170
It also wasn't clear
what China's plan was.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:07.440
It had shut down Wuhan
and had shut down Hubei

00:10:07.440 --> 00:10:10.270
but it was still struggling to communicate

00:10:10.270 --> 00:10:12.660
with the rest of the
world what was going on.

00:10:12.660 --> 00:10:15.470
And it hadn't shut China's borders yet

00:10:15.470 --> 00:10:17.900
to the rest of the world.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.540
With approximately 10,000 confirmed cases

00:10:20.540 --> 00:10:23.890
of COVID in China, the Trump
administration uses travel

00:10:23.890 --> 00:10:27.210
restrictions to limit the
transmission risk from China.

00:10:27.210 --> 00:10:30.093
Any U.S. citizen returning
to the United States

00:10:30.093 --> 00:10:34.760
who has been in Hubei Province
in the previous 14 days

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:39.760
will be subject to up to 14
days of mandatory quarantine.

00:10:39.840 --> 00:10:41.610
The Chinese people together

00:10:41.610 --> 00:10:43.340
with the Chinese government
have gone through

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:46.600
huge difficulties and
made great sacrifices.

00:10:46.600 --> 00:10:49.270
Globally, China has
also fulfilled its duty

00:10:49.270 --> 00:10:51.683
of helping control the
spread of the virus.

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:01.260
While Wuhan would remain
under strict lockdown,

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:04.710
the virus then known
officially as SARS-CoV-2

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:08.960
had jumped to Japan, South
Korea, Australia and Europe.

00:11:08.960 --> 00:11:12.320
It's destructive force
was keenly felt in Italy.

00:11:12.320 --> 00:11:15.230
Specifically it's
business center of Milan.

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:19.130
I went with my kids to the
kindergarten to tell a bunch

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:23.000
of five years old kid, what
does it mean being a journalist.

00:11:23.000 --> 00:11:25.780
And then we left in the evening
to go to my parents place,

00:11:25.780 --> 00:11:27.050
which is near Venice.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:31.260
As soon as we got to the Venice
area, the number of cases

00:11:31.260 --> 00:11:35.943
in Italy had already
jumped from one to dozens.

00:11:35.943 --> 00:11:40.420
And as I was going to bed,
I got a WhatsApp message

00:11:40.420 --> 00:11:44.050
confirming the first Italian fatalities

00:11:44.050 --> 00:11:46.060
related to coronavirus.

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:47.440
Two more people had died

00:11:47.440 --> 00:11:50.240
so, that is 14 deaths in Italy.

00:11:50.240 --> 00:11:54.830
And the number has also jumped,
it is now more than 500.

00:11:54.830 --> 00:11:59.830
There, there was resistance
to impose a strict lockdown

00:12:00.850 --> 00:12:04.420
because it's one of the
industrial hubs of Italy.

00:12:04.420 --> 00:12:07.823
Some leaders were saying
Milan is open for business.

00:12:08.730 --> 00:12:11.100
Failure to quickly take
action would result

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:14.290
in massive deaths at nursing
homes from a complex disease

00:12:14.290 --> 00:12:18.030
the virus causes called COVID-19.

00:12:18.030 --> 00:12:20.520
Milan's hospital system is so overwhelmed

00:12:20.520 --> 00:12:22.950
that makeshift morgues are required.

00:12:22.950 --> 00:12:25.650
Italian prime minister
Giuseppe Conte pushed

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.210
the world's eighth largest
economy with more than

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.710
60 million inhabitants
into virtual quarantine.

00:12:31.710 --> 00:12:34.160
A preview of what was to come in New York,

00:12:34.160 --> 00:12:36.570
Sao Paolo and Mumbai.

00:12:36.570 --> 00:12:40.660
We were the first Western
country to face the pandemic.

00:12:40.660 --> 00:12:45.660
No one had before an experienced
so, we were essentially

00:12:45.670 --> 00:12:48.780
leading the way,
obviously not a great way,

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.903
for the rest of the Western world.

00:12:57.140 --> 00:12:59.770
Even as Italy locked
down, the virus stormed

00:12:59.770 --> 00:13:02.420
across Western Europe
and into the middle East,

00:13:02.420 --> 00:13:04.750
eventually landing on American shores

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:08.010
as outbreaks took hold in
both Seattle and New York.

00:13:08.010 --> 00:13:10.770
But unlike countries like
China and South Korea

00:13:10.770 --> 00:13:13.530
that took swift and dramatic
government led action

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:16.800
to contain the spread of the
virus, President Donald Trump

00:13:16.800 --> 00:13:19.645
downplays the risk and
projects confidence.

00:13:19.645 --> 00:13:23.630
That's the thing that I
still don't fully understand,

00:13:23.630 --> 00:13:28.630
is how come there was a very
clear account of what to do

00:13:29.870 --> 00:13:33.150
to get on top of this that came back

00:13:33.150 --> 00:13:35.890
from this joint mission in China.

00:13:35.890 --> 00:13:40.890
What was it that led so
many countries to conclude

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:45.500
that they would not follow
the lessons from that China

00:13:45.500 --> 00:13:48.660
experience and they would
go about it differently?

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:49.917
Worries about a pandemic at this point?

00:13:49.917 --> 00:13:54.380
No, we're not at all and we
have it totally under control.

00:13:54.380 --> 00:13:57.330
It's one person, coming in from China

00:13:57.330 --> 00:14:01.420
and we have it under control,
it's gonna be just fine.

00:14:01.420 --> 00:14:03.100
He knew that the virus
could be very dangerous.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.560
He'd been told in classified
briefings that this could

00:14:05.560 --> 00:14:09.030
really rip through the nation
and kill a lot of people.

00:14:09.030 --> 00:14:10.570
Jennifer Jacobs is Bloomberg

00:14:10.570 --> 00:14:12.610
Senior White House Reporter.

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:13.930
He didn't wanna be alarmist.

00:14:13.930 --> 00:14:16.980
He didn't want people to
stop going out and shopping

00:14:16.980 --> 00:14:19.493
and to keeping the economy moving forward.

00:14:20.330 --> 00:14:21.792
Mr. President, happy Super Bowl Day.

00:14:21.792 --> 00:14:23.100
Thank you very much yeah, thank you.

00:14:23.100 --> 00:14:26.570
Corona virus, I think we're
now up to our 8th case

00:14:26.570 --> 00:14:28.860
in the United States.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.640
How concerned are you?

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:33.800
Well, we pretty much shut it
down coming in from China.

00:14:33.800 --> 00:14:37.020
We can't have thousands
of people coming in

00:14:37.020 --> 00:14:41.820
who may have this
problem, the Corona virus.

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:44.250
On February 5th, this cases began to show

00:14:44.250 --> 00:14:45.570
in the United States.

00:14:45.570 --> 00:14:49.460
The CDC would send testing kits
to labs around the country.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:52.300
However, soon after those
kits would ultimately prove

00:14:52.300 --> 00:14:55.500
to have a faulty component,
delaying widespread testing

00:14:55.500 --> 00:14:58.120
in the U.S. until March
and allowing the virus

00:14:58.120 --> 00:14:59.710
to spread undetected.

00:14:59.710 --> 00:15:02.653
And New York City would be
the hardest hit early on.

00:15:04.080 --> 00:15:05.140
I'm an attending physician

00:15:05.140 --> 00:15:07.630
at the Mount Sinai Queens Hospital,

00:15:07.630 --> 00:15:12.060
we had over 60 patients
waiting for a hospital bed.

00:15:12.060 --> 00:15:14.590
I'm seeing young people, old patients,

00:15:14.590 --> 00:15:18.380
people of all age ranges who
are just incredibly sick.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:21.600
I can't imagine my family
being here with no one.

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:24.610
So I have to hold their
hand while they pass away,

00:15:24.610 --> 00:15:26.460
at least somebody is there, you know?

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:34.500
Cities around the U.S. moved to lockdowns

00:15:34.500 --> 00:15:37.360
to control the spread and
prevent hospital systems

00:15:37.360 --> 00:15:38.920
from becoming overwhelmed.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:42.420
He started off with these
press briefings back in March

00:15:42.420 --> 00:15:45.060
where he was telling the
public about the coronavirus

00:15:45.060 --> 00:15:46.420
and what they should do.

00:15:46.420 --> 00:15:48.890
We continue to marshall
every resource at America's

00:15:48.890 --> 00:15:51.980
disposal in the fight
against the Chinese virus.

00:15:51.980 --> 00:15:53.960
The President really thrives
in front of the camera,

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.290
it's one of his favorite things to do.

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:58.130
And there was a window of
time when he really had

00:15:58.130 --> 00:15:59.400
the nation's attention.

00:15:59.400 --> 00:16:01.930
We at war and the Crusades were at war.

00:16:01.930 --> 00:16:04.140
But one of his strengths
in front of the camera

00:16:04.140 --> 00:16:05.850
is that he likes to lib.

00:16:05.850 --> 00:16:08.370
I would like you to speak
to the medical doctors

00:16:08.370 --> 00:16:12.790
to see if there's any way
that you can apply light

00:16:12.790 --> 00:16:15.590
and heat to cure.

00:16:15.590 --> 00:16:17.470
And again I say, maybe
he can, maybe he can't,

00:16:17.470 --> 00:16:21.080
I'm not a doctor but I'm like
a person that has a good,

00:16:21.080 --> 00:16:21.913
you know what.

00:16:21.913 --> 00:16:23.930
In public health those officials say,

00:16:23.930 --> 00:16:27.240
if you don't have one
message, one unified message,

00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:28.520
you don't have any message.

00:16:28.520 --> 00:16:30.660
There were a lot of instances
where the government

00:16:30.660 --> 00:16:32.970
just sent mixed signals.

00:16:32.970 --> 00:16:36.920
What I saw not working
well during this pandemic

00:16:36.920 --> 00:16:40.170
was communication and
public health messaging.

00:16:40.170 --> 00:16:45.170
It's very clear that we need
a clear authoritative voice

00:16:47.120 --> 00:16:52.120
that we trust that can
unite us as a country

00:16:52.210 --> 00:16:56.940
and that can guide us with
the best scientific evidence.

00:16:56.940 --> 00:16:59.660
But scientific evidence can change.

00:16:59.660 --> 00:17:02.100
And a lack of clear and
consistent messaging

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:04.870
from The White House would
contribute to face masks

00:17:04.870 --> 00:17:07.440
becoming a divisive political symbol.

00:17:07.440 --> 00:17:11.130
Back in January, the CDC
was saying healthy people

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:12.970
do not need to wear masks.

00:17:12.970 --> 00:17:16.680
The U.S. Surgeon General,
in fact tweeted a message

00:17:16.680 --> 00:17:21.100
in which he said, seriously
people, stop buying masks.

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.560
But then as we learn more about the virus,

00:17:23.560 --> 00:17:28.560
we realize that up to 45%
of patients can be infected

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:33.910
not have any symptoms but
be transmitting that virus

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:35.720
in the respiratory droplets.

00:17:35.720 --> 00:17:39.080
And that was the point when
we said, wait a minute,

00:17:39.080 --> 00:17:41.120
then mask makes sense, right?

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:44.880
Let everyone wear a mask so
that if they're infected,

00:17:44.880 --> 00:17:47.760
then that will contain
those respiratory droplets

00:17:47.760 --> 00:17:50.940
and keep them from transmitting
the virus to other people.

00:17:50.940 --> 00:17:53.840
We were in an evolving situation.

00:17:53.840 --> 00:17:57.930
And when an evolving, unrolling
situation is in effect,

00:17:57.930 --> 00:18:01.420
your information will
evolve and you'll be able

00:18:01.420 --> 00:18:04.973
to make decisions based on
the most recent information.

00:18:06.560 --> 00:18:08.290
The CDC in early April

00:18:08.290 --> 00:18:10.790
put out guidance to wear masks.

00:18:10.790 --> 00:18:14.510
However, Trump would emphasize
it being a personal choice.

00:18:14.510 --> 00:18:16.640
One he often said no to.

00:18:16.640 --> 00:18:21.640
I think wearing a face
mask as great presidents,

00:18:21.650 --> 00:18:25.430
prime ministers, dictators,
kings, queens, I don't know,

00:18:25.430 --> 00:18:28.300
somehow I don't see it for myself.

00:18:28.300 --> 00:18:30.560
And while health officials
and even Democratic

00:18:30.560 --> 00:18:34.020
rival Joe Biden would
emphatically support masks.

00:18:34.020 --> 00:18:36.530
Trump would continue to
avoid being seen in public

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:37.520
wearing one.

00:18:37.520 --> 00:18:39.950
If you are on the left
of the political spectrum

00:18:39.950 --> 00:18:42.470
you're probably very
concerned about healthcare,

00:18:42.470 --> 00:18:44.150
that's probably one of your top issues.

00:18:44.150 --> 00:18:47.370
If you're on the right
side of the ideology,

00:18:47.370 --> 00:18:50.110
maybe your top concerns
are about foreign policy

00:18:50.110 --> 00:18:51.100
or about the economy.

00:18:51.100 --> 00:18:54.350
So there was this innate
divide from the beginning

00:18:54.350 --> 00:18:57.160
about what exactly should
be the top priority.

00:18:57.160 --> 00:19:02.160
And the president just never
really felt that masks were

00:19:02.690 --> 00:19:05.940
going to be a panacea and just
never really encouraged them

00:19:05.940 --> 00:19:09.487
and people especially his
supporters really adopted that

00:19:09.487 --> 00:19:11.650
and that became baked
into the public psyche

00:19:11.650 --> 00:19:15.173
that masks were not necessarily
what they should be doing.

00:19:18.174 --> 00:19:20.127
Can't you read better without an eye?

00:19:20.127 --> 00:19:21.637
No.

00:19:21.637 --> 00:19:24.042
I don't wanna fear you.

00:19:24.042 --> 00:19:26.292
They don't wanna help me.

00:19:27.470 --> 00:19:30.770
By mid April, state and
local state home orders

00:19:30.770 --> 00:19:33.020
have fueled a devastating economic impact

00:19:33.020 --> 00:19:34.890
for many Americans.

00:19:34.890 --> 00:19:38.400
In the harshest downtown for
American workers in history,

00:19:38.400 --> 00:19:42.580
employers cut 20.5 million
jobs pushing the jobless rate

00:19:42.580 --> 00:19:43.873
to nearly 15%.

00:19:49.920 --> 00:19:53.330
And even though Congress
would pass the $2.2 trillion

00:19:53.330 --> 00:19:57.280
Cares Act, the largest economic
recovery package in history,

00:19:57.280 --> 00:20:01.040
large scale rallies would
erupt all around the country.

00:20:01.040 --> 00:20:04.210
We've had enough so, we're practicing.

00:20:04.210 --> 00:20:07.830
What you see is our right to
express our heartfelt feelings.

00:20:07.830 --> 00:20:09.173
We wanna get back to work.

00:20:10.240 --> 00:20:11.410
Trump would show support

00:20:11.410 --> 00:20:13.970
for these rallies tweeting,
Liberate Michigan!

00:20:13.970 --> 00:20:16.660
Liberate Minnesota and Virginia.

00:20:16.660 --> 00:20:19.070
It's an extraordinary
fact that he is siding

00:20:19.070 --> 00:20:21.460
with these anti-lockdown activists

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:24.800
and not with his own scientific advisors.

00:20:24.800 --> 00:20:26.620
So what do I say to the science?

00:20:26.620 --> 00:20:28.390
I say, I don't believe your science

00:20:28.390 --> 00:20:30.100
because I believe my God.

00:20:30.100 --> 00:20:33.260
The denial of reality
because authority tells you

00:20:33.260 --> 00:20:38.260
something, it's stunning,
truly surprised me,

00:20:38.470 --> 00:20:40.340
the depth and the extent of it.

00:20:40.340 --> 00:20:44.630
We have a historic pandemic,
that's ravaging the world

00:20:44.630 --> 00:20:46.900
and in our country and we're not alone,

00:20:46.900 --> 00:20:49.323
some of the European
countries are the same,

00:20:49.323 --> 00:20:52.740
there's a degree of political divisiveness

00:20:52.740 --> 00:20:57.700
that a public health
issue has assumed strong

00:20:57.700 --> 00:21:02.420
political overtones
namely, your one ideology,

00:21:02.420 --> 00:21:05.470
believe one thing, another
ideology believe another.

00:21:05.470 --> 00:21:07.880
Masks work, masks don't work.

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:10.030
It's a hoax, it's real.

00:21:10.030 --> 00:21:14.230
It's just extraordinary
going through this right now,

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:16.013
I think is unprecedented.

00:21:24.040 --> 00:21:27.440
There was Some feeling in The
White House that this virus

00:21:27.440 --> 00:21:31.070
was so contagious that
it was almost inevitable

00:21:31.070 --> 00:21:32.410
that people were going to get it.

00:21:32.410 --> 00:21:35.000
Then at some point, the
Trump administration decided

00:21:35.000 --> 00:21:38.173
that the best message was, let's
just wait for this vaccine.

00:21:39.260 --> 00:21:41.270
In late April Bloomberg breaks news

00:21:41.270 --> 00:21:43.350
of Operation Warp Speed.

00:21:43.350 --> 00:21:46.350
A Manhattan project style,
U.S. government led effort

00:21:46.350 --> 00:21:50.100
to drastically cut the time
needed to develop a vaccine.

00:21:50.100 --> 00:21:53.150
The project's goal was
to have 300 million doses

00:21:53.150 --> 00:21:56.620
of a COVID vaccine by January 2021.

00:21:56.620 --> 00:21:59.750
The Trump administration
absolutely deserves

00:21:59.750 --> 00:22:02.430
a lot of credit for Operation Warp Speed.

00:22:02.430 --> 00:22:05.330
I mean, the amount of
money that was poured in

00:22:05.330 --> 00:22:07.490
by the administration was extraordinary.

00:22:07.490 --> 00:22:10.510
Billions and billions of dollars

00:22:10.510 --> 00:22:12.920
Through Operation Warp Speed, the U.S.

00:22:12.920 --> 00:22:15.950
had a war chest of $18 billion to invest

00:22:15.950 --> 00:22:19.040
in COVID-19 vaccines and treatments.

00:22:19.040 --> 00:22:22.010
The idea back then that a
vaccine would be the way out

00:22:22.010 --> 00:22:24.430
of this was a really
difficult thing to comprehend

00:22:24.430 --> 00:22:26.710
because if you look at
the timelines it takes

00:22:26.710 --> 00:22:29.570
to get vaccines developed
and you know, the majority

00:22:29.570 --> 00:22:31.780
of which are not even successful
but it can take around

00:22:31.780 --> 00:22:34.630
a decade to get a successful
vaccine to market.

00:22:34.630 --> 00:22:36.530
So the idea that you could get a vaccine

00:22:36.530 --> 00:22:39.390
in sort of 12 to 18 month
timeframe that would be sufficient

00:22:39.390 --> 00:22:43.350
to help the world emerge from
this pandemic was quite crazy

00:22:43.350 --> 00:22:44.200
at the beginning.

00:22:50.151 --> 00:22:52.960
In late spring, early summer,
you saw a number of countries

00:22:52.960 --> 00:22:56.250
like the U.K., the U.S. and the
European Union particularly,

00:22:56.250 --> 00:22:58.630
step up and create programs
that would allow them

00:22:58.630 --> 00:23:01.010
to accelerate the
development of the vaccines

00:23:01.010 --> 00:23:04.340
and also fund the vaccines
on a wide ranging platform

00:23:04.340 --> 00:23:06.610
to give multiple shots on
goal for their countries,

00:23:06.610 --> 00:23:08.920
those regions, to have
something successful.

00:23:08.920 --> 00:23:11.170
We saw similar efforts
in China and in Russia

00:23:11.170 --> 00:23:13.450
with their own national
vaccines that they were trialing

00:23:13.450 --> 00:23:16.810
and investing in and funding
for their populations.

00:23:16.810 --> 00:23:19.270
In the past, worldwide vaccine development

00:23:19.270 --> 00:23:21.130
was starved for funding.

00:23:21.130 --> 00:23:24.560
Big pharma and biotech firms
usually focus on more lucrative

00:23:24.560 --> 00:23:27.040
areas like cancer treatments.

00:23:27.040 --> 00:23:29.300
From spring to summer,
a number of vaccines

00:23:29.300 --> 00:23:32.500
would begin trials, particularly
promising with vaccines

00:23:32.500 --> 00:23:35.640
using a new technology
called messenger RNA.

00:23:35.640 --> 00:23:37.170
Being developed by Moderna

00:23:37.170 --> 00:23:39.343
and the Pfizer BioNTech partnership.

00:23:40.400 --> 00:23:43.210
We get this little piece of messenger RNA

00:23:43.210 --> 00:23:45.720
which is relatively unstable,

00:23:45.720 --> 00:23:48.100
that's why we have to keep it frozen.

00:23:48.100 --> 00:23:52.610
We have this messenger
RNA deliver the message

00:23:52.610 --> 00:23:56.880
that the sales need so that
then we can mount a response

00:23:56.880 --> 00:24:01.290
to this virus and in
the end it's destroyed.

00:24:01.290 --> 00:24:03.180
And even though its timeline was slightly

00:24:03.180 --> 00:24:06.580
behind other leading candidates,
a vaccine being developed

00:24:06.580 --> 00:24:09.820
by Oxford scientists and
drug maker AstraZeneca

00:24:09.820 --> 00:24:12.370
would get a lot of early attention.

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:14.550
The AstraZeneca/Oxford vaccine has really

00:24:14.550 --> 00:24:17.430
had an outsize impact on supply agreements

00:24:17.430 --> 00:24:20.260
because not only can it be
stored at refrigerator conditions

00:24:20.260 --> 00:24:23.500
which makes it much more
conducive to be deployed

00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:26.160
to the developing world but it also,

00:24:26.160 --> 00:24:28.500
is gonna be sold at cost during
the period of the pandemic

00:24:28.500 --> 00:24:31.770
which makes it much more feasible
for countries to purchase

00:24:31.770 --> 00:24:33.760
huge doses of the vaccine.

00:24:33.760 --> 00:24:36.090
So when you're thinking
about which horse to back,

00:24:36.090 --> 00:24:38.850
AstraZeneca/Oxford was a really
good bet at the beginning

00:24:38.850 --> 00:24:42.740
of the pandemic for both
success, deployment, cost,

00:24:42.740 --> 00:24:44.610
and just the potential
to be really effective

00:24:44.610 --> 00:24:45.760
in ending the pandemic.

00:24:53.550 --> 00:24:55.940
As scientists rush to develop a vaccine,

00:24:55.940 --> 00:24:59.310
a summer surge of cases emerges worldwide.

00:24:59.310 --> 00:25:01.650
Any hope that warmer
weather would tame the virus

00:25:01.650 --> 00:25:02.710
is dashed.

00:25:02.710 --> 00:25:05.190
As it continued its rampage across Europe

00:25:05.190 --> 00:25:08.370
and the developing world,
particularly India, Brazil

00:25:08.370 --> 00:25:09.453
and South Africa.

00:25:10.770 --> 00:25:13.480
However China's strict
lockdowns have allowed for life

00:25:13.480 --> 00:25:16.030
to return to normal for many citizens.

00:25:16.030 --> 00:25:18.880
Back in the United States,
while cases in the Northeast

00:25:18.880 --> 00:25:22.070
stabilized, premature lifting
of lockdowns caused a spike

00:25:22.070 --> 00:25:23.623
of cases in the sunbelt.

00:25:24.850 --> 00:25:28.760
And by September, Midwest States
experienced a dramatic rise

00:25:28.760 --> 00:25:32.080
in COVID-19 cases with South Dakota alone

00:25:32.080 --> 00:25:36.430
having a 166% increase and 10 other States

00:25:36.430 --> 00:25:39.320
reporting record one day increases.

00:25:39.320 --> 00:25:42.010
The annual Sturgis
Motorcycle Rally, school

00:25:42.010 --> 00:25:45.850
and university reopenings and
Labor Day weekend celebrations

00:25:45.850 --> 00:25:48.130
have all been cited as case links.

00:25:48.130 --> 00:25:50.700
Yet nobody was quite
expecting a viral outbreak

00:25:50.700 --> 00:25:52.663
in the West wing of The White House.

00:25:54.130 --> 00:25:57.330
When I heard that Hope
Hicks, one of the President's

00:25:57.330 --> 00:26:01.270
closest advisors had the
virus, we immediately started

00:26:01.270 --> 00:26:04.200
thinking it's possible
that the President had it.

00:26:04.200 --> 00:26:06.730
Word has come that one
of President Trump's

00:26:06.730 --> 00:26:10.870
closest aides, Hope
Hicks has tested positive

00:26:10.870 --> 00:26:15.490
for Corona virus and in fact
is apparently quite sick.

00:26:15.490 --> 00:26:18.300
The fact that we reported
on Hope's illness,

00:26:18.300 --> 00:26:21.100
sent a signal to The White
House that we've got deep

00:26:21.100 --> 00:26:23.880
sourcing that they probably
can't hide this from us.

00:26:23.880 --> 00:26:27.220
That no matter what happens,
someone is gonna find out.

00:26:27.220 --> 00:26:29.270
And I know that people think
that there was a good chance

00:26:29.270 --> 00:26:33.220
that if we hadn't reported
on Hope Hicks's diagnosis,

00:26:33.220 --> 00:26:35.200
that it's possible we
never would have known

00:26:35.200 --> 00:26:36.740
about the President's diagnosis.

00:26:36.740 --> 00:26:39.840
The President of the United
States now confirming

00:26:39.840 --> 00:26:43.250
to the world that he and the
first lady of the United States

00:26:43.250 --> 00:26:46.620
have both tested positive
for the coronavirus

00:26:46.620 --> 00:26:48.800
and they will quarantine.

00:26:48.800 --> 00:26:51.310
President Trump received Dexamethasone,

00:26:51.310 --> 00:26:54.590
Remdesivir and a cocktail
of therapeutic antibodies

00:26:54.590 --> 00:26:57.550
from drug maker Regeneron
that was not yet available

00:26:57.550 --> 00:26:58.940
to the public.

00:26:58.940 --> 00:27:02.350
At the same time, more
officials were testing positive.

00:27:02.350 --> 00:27:04.490
Breaking news, it's fair
to say there is an outbreak

00:27:04.490 --> 00:27:05.450
within The White House.

00:27:05.450 --> 00:27:09.350
Kellyanne Conway has tested
positive for the Corona virus.

00:27:09.350 --> 00:27:11.700
Governor Chris Christie now reports

00:27:11.700 --> 00:27:13.980
that he has tested positive.

00:27:13.980 --> 00:27:15.470
Stephen Miller, a senior aide

00:27:15.470 --> 00:27:18.750
to President Trump has become
the 24th person connected

00:27:18.750 --> 00:27:21.930
to The White House to test
positive for COVID-19.

00:27:21.930 --> 00:27:23.960
There was a very much
worry about it spreading

00:27:23.960 --> 00:27:25.440
throughout the entire West wing.

00:27:25.440 --> 00:27:27.540
There was worry about his
re-election prospects.

00:27:27.540 --> 00:27:30.690
There was worry about how
this was going to affect

00:27:30.690 --> 00:27:34.720
their entire plan until
the November 3rd election.

00:27:34.720 --> 00:27:36.870
But after several days in Walter Reed,

00:27:36.870 --> 00:27:38.530
President Trump would be released

00:27:38.530 --> 00:27:40.440
and would return to The White House.

00:27:40.440 --> 00:27:41.490
Walking out on his own,

00:27:41.490 --> 00:27:43.610
this image over to getting
attention back at The White House

00:27:43.610 --> 00:27:47.200
tonight appearing eager to take
off that mask and signaling

00:27:47.200 --> 00:27:49.650
tonight he'll be back at
the campaign trail soon.

00:27:58.250 --> 00:28:00.720
However, just a little over a month later,

00:28:00.720 --> 00:28:03.200
in a record breaking election turnout,

00:28:03.200 --> 00:28:06.160
Trump would lose to democratic
challenger, Joe Biden.

00:28:06.160 --> 00:28:08.640
Here's your final tally
in the electoral college,

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:10.150
this is for the history books, Wolf.

00:28:10.150 --> 00:28:12.590
306 electoral votes for Joe Biden,

00:28:12.590 --> 00:28:15.690
232 electoral votes for Donald Trump.

00:28:15.690 --> 00:28:17.880
As you noted, that is an exact reversal

00:28:17.880 --> 00:28:19.420
of what it was four years ago.

00:28:19.420 --> 00:28:24.330
His advisors do know that the
handling of the coronavirus

00:28:24.330 --> 00:28:26.390
by The White House and
by the President himself

00:28:26.390 --> 00:28:29.930
and his refusal to model some
of the public health measures

00:28:29.930 --> 00:28:33.080
that could have at least put
a dent in the coronavirus,

00:28:33.080 --> 00:28:35.350
probably killed his re-election.

00:28:35.350 --> 00:28:37.750
As Trump's legal team
aggressively challenged

00:28:37.750 --> 00:28:40.400
the election's outcome,
there were huge developments

00:28:40.400 --> 00:28:41.980
on the vaccine front.

00:28:41.980 --> 00:28:44.530
On November 9th, the
Pfizer/BioNTech vaccine

00:28:44.530 --> 00:28:48.430
reported to show a more
than 90% efficacy rating.

00:28:48.430 --> 00:28:53.430
A week later Moderna's vaccine
would report 94.5% efficacy.

00:28:53.750 --> 00:28:58.750
I was saying, boy, I'll take
a 70% effective vaccine,

00:28:59.080 --> 00:29:03.100
65% effective vaccine,
it will be very helpful.

00:29:03.100 --> 00:29:06.180
It won't crush the outbreak
but it'd be very helpful.

00:29:06.180 --> 00:29:11.180
To get 95% effective
vaccines from two candidates

00:29:12.840 --> 00:29:17.110
that were the same platform
but different companies,

00:29:17.110 --> 00:29:21.970
with essentially identical
results, 94%, 95% efficacy,

00:29:21.970 --> 00:29:25.370
I was overwhelmingly pleasantly surprised

00:29:25.370 --> 00:29:26.420
that that was the case.

00:29:26.420 --> 00:29:28.913
So, that's the one
thing I did not predict.

00:29:35.790 --> 00:29:37.510
In the first week of December,

00:29:37.510 --> 00:29:40.170
the U.K. was the first
declare the use of a new shot

00:29:40.170 --> 00:29:42.840
from Pfizer Inc and BioNTech SE.

00:29:42.840 --> 00:29:45.660
The U.S. would do the same a week later.

00:29:45.660 --> 00:29:48.340
The approval of Moderna's
vaccine would follow later

00:29:48.340 --> 00:29:49.810
in the month.

00:29:49.810 --> 00:29:52.920
Not long after, people aged
80 and over in the U.K.

00:29:52.920 --> 00:29:55.230
began receiving the vaccine.

00:29:55.230 --> 00:29:57.860
The U.K. as the first
doses of the corona vaccine

00:29:57.860 --> 00:29:59.400
are being injected into patients.

00:29:59.400 --> 00:30:02.530
The country's mass national
vaccination program

00:30:02.530 --> 00:30:05.720
has officially began and
to put this into context,

00:30:05.720 --> 00:30:07.630
this comes less than a year

00:30:07.630 --> 00:30:10.520
after the first case of COVID-19.

00:30:10.520 --> 00:30:12.500
Vaccines being shipped
to healthcare workers

00:30:12.500 --> 00:30:14.180
came as a welcome relief.

00:30:14.180 --> 00:30:18.100
As the U.S. death toll surpasses 325,000.

00:30:18.100 --> 00:30:20.910
Global deaths top 1.7 million.

00:30:20.910 --> 00:30:23.530
And reports of a new
variant out of the U.K.

00:30:23.530 --> 00:30:26.130
show some mutations that
appear to make the virus

00:30:26.130 --> 00:30:27.653
even more contagious.

00:30:28.720 --> 00:30:32.100
By the end of 2020, millions
of people were expected

00:30:32.100 --> 00:30:33.630
to be inoculated.

00:30:33.630 --> 00:30:37.960
By the end of 2021 public health
officials in some countries

00:30:37.960 --> 00:30:42.660
aim to have 60% to 70% of
that populations immunized,

00:30:42.660 --> 00:30:45.311
yet skeptics say that may be a challenge.

00:30:45.311 --> 00:30:47.320
I think we're gonna be
far short of the vaccine

00:30:47.320 --> 00:30:50.190
we're gonna need in the
first two to three quarters

00:30:50.190 --> 00:30:51.630
of next year in the United States.

00:30:51.630 --> 00:30:53.400
I think that's still gonna be a challenge.

00:30:53.400 --> 00:30:56.320
And there's the logistics
and distribution.

00:30:56.320 --> 00:30:58.120
Then there's finding the money,

00:30:58.120 --> 00:31:02.050
then there's all the
coordination, it's just a big job.

00:31:02.050 --> 00:31:07.050
And having seen the challenges
that world leaders have faced

00:31:07.260 --> 00:31:12.110
in actually dealing with the
infection and trying to find

00:31:12.110 --> 00:31:16.910
a way to work on the infection,
I'm thinking they will also

00:31:16.910 --> 00:31:19.373
face challenges with the immunization.

00:31:20.520 --> 00:31:22.170
And even if the rollout of the vaccine

00:31:22.170 --> 00:31:24.540
in the U.S. and the world goes swimmingly,

00:31:24.540 --> 00:31:26.640
it brings up an entirely new problem.

00:31:26.640 --> 00:31:29.590
I think we have kind of a
double-edged sword challenge

00:31:29.590 --> 00:31:32.450
of early on we're gonna
have many early adopters

00:31:32.450 --> 00:31:35.180
that want the vaccine and we're
not gonna have nearly enough

00:31:35.180 --> 00:31:36.970
which is gonna create its own crisis.

00:31:36.970 --> 00:31:40.180
Followed by what I'm afraid
will be vaccines sitting there

00:31:40.180 --> 00:31:41.470
waiting to find a arm.

00:31:41.470 --> 00:31:45.160
About a 1/4 of Americans do
not wanna get vaccinated.

00:31:45.160 --> 00:31:48.000
The skepticism represents
a challenge as the country

00:31:48.000 --> 00:31:50.710
tries to control exploding infections,

00:31:50.710 --> 00:31:52.300
hospitalizations and deaths.

00:31:52.300 --> 00:31:54.660
Many are wary of the
vaccine's unprecedented

00:31:54.660 --> 00:31:58.610
speed, others are polarized by politics.

00:31:58.610 --> 00:32:03.160
The depth of the scientific
hostility to science,

00:32:03.160 --> 00:32:07.390
anti-science, which
spills over into anti-vac,

00:32:07.390 --> 00:32:08.883
truly surprised me.

00:32:10.070 --> 00:32:12.650
There are certain regions of
the country where in the very

00:32:12.650 --> 00:32:15.970
towns, counties, cities,
where the hospitals

00:32:15.970 --> 00:32:20.490
are being overrun with COVID-19 patients,

00:32:20.490 --> 00:32:23.640
there are people in that
area, which are still saying

00:32:23.640 --> 00:32:27.390
it's a hoax, it's fake
news, it doesn't exist.

00:32:27.390 --> 00:32:30.170
It's mind boggling to see that.

00:32:30.170 --> 00:32:32.930
The U.S. and U.K. have
reserved enough vaccines

00:32:32.930 --> 00:32:36.930
to inoculate between 150% and nearly 300%

00:32:36.930 --> 00:32:39.430
of their population.

00:32:39.430 --> 00:32:43.130
But poorer countries like
Vietnam, Ukraine and Uganda,

00:32:43.130 --> 00:32:46.990
so far only have enough allocated
to them to cover about 5%

00:32:46.990 --> 00:32:49.890
of their populations under
an international vaccine

00:32:49.890 --> 00:32:51.490
acquisition group.

00:32:51.490 --> 00:32:56.490
I want to ask all world
leaders to ask themselves,

00:32:56.650 --> 00:32:59.490
are they viewing this
from a truly international

00:32:59.490 --> 00:33:03.180
perspective or are they
viewing it from a parochial

00:33:03.180 --> 00:33:05.440
national perspective?

00:33:05.440 --> 00:33:08.070
Ultimately, the impact
of COVID will be felt

00:33:08.070 --> 00:33:11.540
for years to come and how
leaders around the world

00:33:11.540 --> 00:33:14.490
not only learn from this
past year but preparing

00:33:14.490 --> 00:33:18.133
future years will determine the
extent of the next outbreak.

00:33:19.630 --> 00:33:24.380
It's not if but when the
next pandemic occurs.

00:33:24.380 --> 00:33:29.380
We do understand how
important it is to be prepared

00:33:29.470 --> 00:33:31.690
and hopefully we will
take the necessary steps

00:33:31.690 --> 00:33:33.333
to be prepared.

00:33:36.080 --> 00:33:38.300
We need to push the science

00:33:38.300 --> 00:33:40.880
and we need to follow scientific advice.

00:33:40.880 --> 00:33:45.860
We need to learn to trust
our public health officials

00:33:45.860 --> 00:33:49.530
and we need to have that
united voice moving forward.

00:33:49.530 --> 00:33:52.370
So that hopefully in future pandemics,

00:33:52.370 --> 00:33:54.983
we won't be divided as a country.

00:33:56.390 --> 00:33:58.150
While many things went wrong throughout

00:33:58.150 --> 00:34:01.040
the year, when it comes to
COVID, there are still victories

00:34:01.040 --> 00:34:03.570
that warrant cautious optimism.

00:34:03.570 --> 00:34:06.760
I think one of the things
that we did do right

00:34:06.760 --> 00:34:11.500
was getting a vaccine into patients.

00:34:11.500 --> 00:34:14.860
I am totally impressed by
the way in which scientists

00:34:14.860 --> 00:34:18.420
everywhere have cooperated
like never before

00:34:18.420 --> 00:34:19.590
on the vaccination.

00:34:19.590 --> 00:34:23.610
And also, honestly I wanted
to say that the companies

00:34:23.610 --> 00:34:25.820
have done pretty well too.

00:34:25.820 --> 00:34:28.610
We will need a lot more of that kind

00:34:28.610 --> 00:34:32.850
of radical collaboration
for the vaccination process.

00:34:32.850 --> 00:34:36.290
Not only do we have to
continue doing what we've done

00:34:36.290 --> 00:34:40.750
but we have to actually
redouble our efforts to stretch

00:34:40.750 --> 00:34:44.350
our collaboration potential
for the sake of the future

00:34:44.350 --> 00:34:45.700
of humanity quite honestly.

